hadiths[493]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1009","""Salam is a gift for our community and a protection for our dhimmis."
"1010","""The one who backbites and the one who listens to backbiting are both partners in sin."
"1011","""The atonement for the one you have backbitten is that you seek forgiveness for him."
"1012","""The envious person and the tale-bearer have no connection with me."
"1013","""Anger is from Satan, and Satan was created from fire, and fire is extinguished with water, so when any of you becomes angry, he should perform ablution (wudu)."
"1014","""Anger is a burning coal that burns in the heart of the son of Adam."
"1015","""A believer is quick to become angry and quick to become pleased."
"1016","""The best people of my Ummah are those who, if they become angry, then turn back from it."
"1017","""The greatest betrayal is that you say something to your brother, he believes you, but you are lying to him."
"1018","""Avoid lying, for lying leads one away from faith."
"1019","""Do not drink in one go like a camel, rather drink in two or three sips, and when you begin to drink, say Bismillah, and when you finish and get up, say Alhamdulillah."
"1020","""Do not walk ahead of him (i.e., your father), do not sit before him, and do not call him by his name."
"1021","""Of all sins, Allah delays the punishment for whichever He wills until the Day of Resurrection, except for disobedience to parents; indeed, Allah gives the disobedient to parents their punishment in this world before death."
"1022","“Indeed, through charity and maintaining family ties, Allah Almighty increases lifespan and protects from a bad death.”"
"1023","""Allah Almighty, through the blessing of maintaining family ties, prospers the regions of people and increases their wealth."
"1024","""Whoever possesses three qualities, Allah Almighty will take an easy account from him and will admit him to Paradise by His mercy (and they are): Give to the one who deprives you, maintain ties with the one who severs relations with you, and forgive the one who wrongs you."
"1025","""When one meets his brother upon returning from Jumu'ah, he should say «تقبل الله منا و منك» , meaning: May Allah accept (it) from us and from you."
"1026","""Give gifts to each other, for they create love and remove malice."
"1027","""Give gifts to one another, surely gifts remove diseases and doubts from the heart."
"1028","""Shake hands with one another; this will remove malice and deceit from your hearts."
"1029","""When two Muslims shake hands upon meeting and praise Allah and seek His forgiveness, Allah forgives them."
"1030","""When a believer shakes hands with another believer, a hundred mercies descend upon them both."
"1031","""Do not quarrel with your Muslim brother, do not mock him, and do not make a promise to him which you then break."
"1032","""Two traits cannot be combined in a believer: miserliness and bad character."
"1033","""A deceitful, miserly, and ill-mannered person will not enter Paradise."
"1034","“Misfortune is due to bad temper.”"
"1035","""The Prophet (peace be upon him) used to recite (this supplication) when looking in the mirror: «اللهم كما حسنت خلقي فحسن خلقي» That is, O Allah, just as You have made my physical form beautiful, make my character beautiful as well."
"1036","""Whoever young person honors an elder because of his age, Allah Almighty will appoint someone who will honor him in his old age."
"1037","“One day the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was sitting when his foster father came, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) spread a part of his garment for him and he sat on it. Then his foster mother came, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) spread his garment from the other side and she sat on it. Then his foster brother came, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up for him and seated him in front of himself.”"
"1038","""Only a donkey denies honor and respect."
"1039","""If modesty were a person, it would be a good person, and if shamelessness were a person, it would be a bad person."
"1040","""Cursed is the person on the blessed tongue of the Prophet (peace be upon him) who sits in the middle of a gathering."
"1041","""The beauty of a person is the eloquence of his tongue."
"1042","""Relate only those of my hadiths before my followers which their intellects are able to comprehend."
"1043","""Whenever the Prophet (peace be upon him) narrated a hadith, he would smile."
"1044","""I am neither from play and amusement, nor does play and amusement have any relation to me."
"1045","""Do not frighten a Muslim, for frightening a Muslim is a great injustice."
"1046","""After the obligatory duties, the most beloved deed to Allah Almighty is to bring happiness to a Muslim."
"1047","""Whoever brings happiness to a Muslim household, Allah Almighty will be pleased to grant him Paradise in return."
"1048","""The Prophet (peace be upon him) never yawned."
"1049","""Allah Almighty dislikes raising the voice at the time of sneezing and yawning."
"1050","""Whoever sneezes or burps, or hears someone sneeze or burp and says: «الحمد لله على كل حال من الاحوال» , then Allah Almighty will remove seventy diseases from him, the lightest of which is leprosy."
"1051","""Whenever a Muslim sneezes and says «الحمد لله» , Allah Almighty creates an angel from his sneeze who continues to praise Allah until the Day of Resurrection."
"1052","""Beware of being naked, for there is one with you who never leaves you (i.e., the angel), except at the time of relieving oneself and when a man is intimate with his wife."
"1053","""The people of Paradise will speak in Arabic."
"1054","""None of these three things are saved: suspicion, bad omen, and envy."
"1055","""Just as it is a right to reply to a greeting, it is also a right to reply to a letter."
"1056","""Whoever looks at his brother's letter without permission, it is as if he has looked into the fire."
"1057","""The world is carrion, and its seekers are dogs."
"1058","""Whoever possesses an abundance of things will have more preoccupations; whoever has more preoccupations will have greater greed; whoever has greater greed will have more anxiety; and whoever has more anxiety will become heedless of his Lord."
"1059","""If you wish to meet Allah the Exalted in such a state that He is pleased with you, then do not conceal what has been given to you, and do not withhold what you are asked for."
"1060","""Whoever begins his morning with concern for the world has no connection with Allah Almighty."
"1061","""There is no good in a person who does not accumulate wealth for maintaining ties of kinship, fulfilling trusts, and being independent of the creation of Allah."
"1062","""May Allah curse the poor person who humbles himself before a rich man merely because of his wealth."
"1063","""Whoever shows humility before a wealthy person merely because of his wealth, two-thirds of his religion is lost."
"1064","""The key for every nation is there, and the key to Paradise is the poor and needy; these people will be in the assembly of Allah on the Day of Resurrection."
"1065","""Meet Me with your intentions, not with your deeds."
"1066","""Do not look at the smallness of the disobedience, but look at the greatness of the One Whom you are disobeying."
"1067","""Avoid places of suspicion."
"1068","""When a servant shows humility, Allah Almighty raises him towards the seventh heaven."
"1069","""Become strong and tough, practice archery, and walk barefoot."
"1070","""Supplication is the essence of worship."
"1071","""Do not show weakness in supplicating, for no one is ever destroyed by making supplication."
"1072","""Supplication is the weapon of the believer, the pillar of religion, and the light of the heavens and the earth."
"1073","""It is not permissible for a person to lead people in prayer and then supplicate only for himself, leaving out others; if he does so, he has certainly betrayed the people."
"1074","""Let each of you ask his Lord for all his needs, even if the strap of his sandal breaks, he should ask Him for that as well."
"1075","""When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would raise his hands for supplication, he would not lower them until he had passed them over his face."
"1076","""Spread the inner sides of your palms when you ask (in supplication); do not ask with the outer sides, and when you finish (the supplication), wipe your palms over your faces."
"1077","""Indeed, Allah Almighty loves those who persist in supplication."
"1078","The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When Allah returns the soul to a servant (in the morning), and then he recites this supplication «لا اله الا الله وحده لا شريك له له الملك وله الحمد وهو على كل شىء قدير» , Allah forgives all his sins, even if they are as much as the foam of the sea."
"1079","""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever recites this supplication upon waking from sleep: «الحمد لله الذى خلق النوم واليقظة ، الحمد لله الذى بعثنى سالما سويا ، أشهد أن الله يحى الموتى وهو على كل شىء قدير» Allah Almighty says in response that My servant has spoken the truth."
"1080","""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) advised a man to recite Surah Al-Hashr before sleeping, and he (peace and blessings be upon him) said that if (you recite this Surah and) die, you will attain the death of a martyr."
"1081","The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever recites this supplication in the morning has expressed gratitude for that day, and whoever recites it in the evening has expressed gratitude for that night."
"1082","The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever recites this supplication once in the morning or evening: «اللهم انى اصبحت اشهدك واشهد حملة عرشك و ملائكتك و جميع خلقك ، أنت الله لا اله الا انت وأن محمدا عبدك ورسولك» , Allah will free one fourth of him from the Hellfire. Whoever recites this supplication twice, Allah will free half of him from the Hellfire. Whoever recites it three times, Allah will free three fourths of him from the Hellfire. And if someone recites it four times, Allah will (completely) free him from the Hellfire."
"1083","The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Whoever recites these verses in the morning: «فسبحان الله حين تمسون وحين تصبحون ، وله الحمد فى السموات والارض وعشيا وحين تظهرون ، يخرج الحي من الميت ويخرج الميت من الحي ويحي الارض بعد موتها وكذلك تخرجون» then whatever goodness and blessings he has missed that day, he will attain it; and whoever recites these verses in the evening, then whatever goodness and blessings he has missed, he will attain it."
"1084","""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever recites this supplication in the morning will remain protected until the evening, and whoever recites it in the evening will remain protected until the morning. «سبحان الله وبحمده لا قوة الا بالله ما شاء الله كان وما لم يشأ لم يكن» ."
"1085","The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Whoever recites «اعوز بالله السميع العليم من الشيطان الرجيم» three times in the morning and then recites the last three verses of Surah Al-Hashr, Allah will appoint seventy thousand angels for him who will pray for him until the evening, and if he dies during that day, he will attain the rank of martyrdom. And whoever says this in the evening, the same will be done for him until the morning."
"1086","""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Every day when the servants enter the morning, a caller (from Allah) calls out in a loud voice that «سبحان الملك القدوس» and in another narration it is stated: Every morning a caller calls out: O all creatures! Glorify (Allah), the Sovereign, the Most Holy."
"1087","""In one narration, it is stated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say these words in the morning, «أصبحنا وأصبح الملك لله والحمد لله والكبرياء والعظمة لله والخلق والأمر واليل والنهار وما سكن فيهما لله ، اللهم اجعل أول هذا النهار صلاحا و أوسطه نجاحا واخره فلاحا ، يا أرحم الراحمين»"
"1088","""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to recite this supplication morning and evening « اللَّهُمَّ إِنِّي أَسْأَلُكَ مِنْ فَجْأَةِ الْخَيْرِ ، وَأَعُوذُ بِكَ مِنْ فَجْأَةِ الشَّرِّ » ."
"1089","“To be protected from calamities and misfortunes, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) taught a man this supplication to recite in the morning: «باسم الله على نفسى وأهلي ومالي فانه لا يذهب لك شىء» .”"
"1090","""In one narration, it is stated that whoever recites this supplication three times before the Fajr prayer on the morning of Friday, «استغفر الله الذى لا إله إلا هو الحي القيوم و أتوب إليه» , all his sins will be forgiven, even if they are as much as the foam of the sea."
"1091","“When Hazrat Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) complained of sleeplessness to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) taught him this supplication: «اللهم غارت النجوم وهدأت العيون وأنت حي قيوم لا تأخذك سنة ولا نوم يا حي يا قيوم أهدىء ليلى وانى عيني» .”"
"1092","""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to recite this supplication when entering the toilet: «اللهم أني أعوذبك من الرجس النجس الخبيث المخبث : الشيطان الرجيم» ."
"1093","""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to recite this supplication when coming out of the toilet... « اَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِيْ اَذْهَبَ عَنِّي الْاَذٰي وَعَافَانِيْْ » ."
"1094","""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to recite this supplication when coming out of the toilet... «الحمد لله الذى أذاقني لذته وأبقي فى قوته ودفع عني أذاه» ."
"1095","""After completing ablution, one should look towards the sky and recite this supplication: «أشهد أن لا اله الا الله وحده لا شريك له وأشهد أن محمدا عبده ورسوله» ."
"1096","""In response to «حي على الفلاح» , the Prophet (peace be upon him) would say these words: «اللهم اجعلنا من المفلحين» ."
"1097","""In one narration, it is stated that if you see someone reciting poetry in the mosque, curse him three times «فض الله فاك» that is, may Allah break your mouth."
"1098","""Whoever recites Ayat al-Kursi after the obligatory prayer will be in Allah's protection until the next prayer."
"1099","""In one narration, it is mentioned that after finishing the prayer, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would wipe his right hand over his forehead and say: «أشهد أن لا اله الا الله الرحمن الرحيم ، اللهم أذهب عنى الهم والحزن» ."
"1100","""In one narration, it is mentioned that Hazrat Ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) used to recite this supplication at the time of breaking the fast: «اللهم انى أسألك برحمتك التى وسعت كل شىء أن تغفرلي» ."
"1101","""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say this at the time of encountering the enemy: «يا مالك يوم الدين اياك نعبد واياك أستعين» ."
"1102","""In one narration, these words of greeting are present: «وعليك السلام ورحمة االله وبركاته ومغفرته ورضوانه» ."
"1103","""When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would enter the house, he used to recite this supplication: «اللهم أني أسألك خير المولج و خير المخرج بسم الله ولجنا وبسم الله خرجنا وعلي الله ربنا توكلنا» ."
"1104","""When strong winds blew, the Prophet (peace be upon him) would sit down on his knees and supplicate: «اللهم اجعلها رحمة ولا تجعلها عذابا ، اللهم اجعلها رياحا ولا تجعلها ريحا» ."
"1105","""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would recite this supplication upon hearing the sound of thunder: «اللهم لا تقتلنا بغضبك ولا تهلكنا بعذابك وعافنا قبل ذٰلك » ."
"1106","""When the Prophet (peace be upon him) was troubled by a matter, he would look up towards the sky and say: « سبحان الله وبحمده» ."
"1107","""In one narration it is stated that when a person is overwhelmed by any task, he should recite this supplication: «حسبي الله ونعم الوكيل » ."
"1108","""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When you see a flame of fire, say «الله اكبر» , for indeed saying Takbir will extinguish it."
"1109","""When you visit a sick person, ask him to pray for you, for his prayer is like the prayer of the angels."
"1110","""According to the saying of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, whoever recites this supplication when wearing new clothes «الحمد لله الذى كساني ما اواري به عورتي وأتجمل به فى حياتي» will come under the protection of Allah."
"1111","The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the people of my Ummah board a boat, they can be saved from drowning if they recite this supplication: «بسم الله مجريها و مرساها ان ربي لغفور رحيم ، وما قدروا الله حق قدره . . .» ."
"1112","""In one narration, it is mentioned that when Hazrat Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) drank Zamzam water, he would recite this supplication: «اللهم اني أسألك علما نافعا ورزقا واسعا وشفاء من كل داء» ."
"1113","""Shall I not tell you about your illness and its cure? Beware! Your illness is sins and your cure is seeking forgiveness."
"1114","""Whoever makes istighfar (seeking forgiveness) necessary upon himself, Allah Almighty will provide him a way out from every difficulty, will remove his every sorrow, and will grant him from where he could never have imagined."
"1115","""Whoever seeks forgiveness (after committing a sin) has not persisted in the sin, even if he commits the sin seventy times in a day."
"1116","""Whoever did not send blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), his ablution is not valid."
"1117","""Whoever sends blessings upon me eighty (80) times on Friday, Allah Almighty will forgive his sins of eighty (80) years."
"1118","""Sending blessings upon the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) is better than freeing a slave."
"1119","""When you send blessings upon me, include everyone."
"1120","""Adorn your gatherings by sending blessings upon me, for indeed your sending blessings upon me will be a source of light for you on the Day of Judgment."
"1121","""Blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) are not rejected."
"1122","""Whoever sends blessings upon me forty times every Friday, Allah Almighty erases forty years of his sins."
"1123","""When the Friend of Allah (that is, Ibrahim, peace be upon him) and I are mentioned, then (first) send blessings upon him and then upon me; and when (other) prophets are mentioned, then (first) send blessings upon me and then upon them."
"1124","""Indeed, Allah Almighty has sent me as a mercy and guidance for the worlds, and He has commanded me to eliminate musical instruments."
"1125","""Music sows hypocrisy in the heart just as water makes vegetation grow."
"1126","""Whoever listens attentively to a female singer, molten lead will be poured into his ears on the Day of Judgment."
"1127","""Music is the incantation of adultery."
"1128","""The one who plays the flute while alive does not remain happy."
"1129","""Whoever listens attentively to the sound of singing will not be permitted to hear the voices of the spiritual beings in Paradise."
"1130","(Abu Barzah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that we were with the Prophet (peace be upon him) when he heard the sound of singing, so he said, ""See what this is?"" Upon this, I climbed up and saw that Muawiyah and Amr bin Al-As were singing. I informed the Prophet (peace be upon him) of this, so he prayed against them, saying:) ""O Allah! Put them in trial and push them into the Fire."
"1131","""Allah Almighty has cursed singing and those who sing."
"1132","""Without a doubt, love is an expiation for sins."
"1133","(One day Ibn Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) said to his companions: Do you know what is the meaning of this hadith, ""Whoever attributes a lie to me, let him take his place in Hell""? A man fell in love with a woman. One evening, he came to the woman's family and said, ""I am the messenger of the Prophet (peace be upon him). The Prophet (peace be upon him) has sent me to you so that I may stay in whichever of your houses I wish."" He waited for the evening. One of them went to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and said, ""So-and-so has come to us and says that you have ordered him to spend the night in whichever of our houses he wishes."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""He has lied. O so-and-so, go with this man, and if Allah gives you power over him, kill him and burn him in the fire. But I think death will suffice for him."" Then it started to rain from the sky. He went outside to perform ablution, and a snake bit him. When the Prophet (peace be upon him) was informed of this, he said, ""He is in Hell."
"1134","""Do not seek counsel from lovers; they have no opinion. Beware! Their hearts are burned and their intellects have been taken away."
"1135","""Love for something makes one blind and deaf."
"1136","""The gatherings of those who love never diminish."
"1137","""Remove those limits which you find the ability to remove."
"1138","""Remove the punishments from the Muslims as much as you are able."
"1139","""When the prescribed punishment is carried out on the thief, then the liability for the property is no longer upon him."
"1140","""If a woman becomes an apostate, do not kill her."
"1141","""The faces of the wicked will be lashed by flames in the Fire."
"1142","""Do not commit adultery; the pleasure of your women will be lost."
"1143","""Whoever commits adultery with a Jewish or Christian woman, Allah Almighty will burn him in the grave."
"1144","""Allah Almighty will not look with mercy on the Day of Resurrection at the one who commits adultery with his neighbor's wife, nor will He purify him, and He will say to him, 'Enter along with those who are entering Hell.'"
"1145","""Whoever commits adultery has committed adultery with that very thing, even if it is with the wall of his own house."
"1146","“The offspring of adultery will be raised on the Day of Resurrection in the form of monkeys and pigs.”"
"1147","""Whoever spent one dirham for adultery has lost six hundred dirhams."
"1148","""After the death of his son Abū Shahmah, Hazrat Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) carried out the prescribed punishment on him."
"1149","""If a sodomite (one who commits acts with boys) dies without repentance, he is transformed into the form of a pig in the grave."
"1150","""Whoever kisses a boy out of lust, Allah curses him; if he shakes hands with him out of lust, his prayer is not accepted; if he embraces him out of lust, he will be beaten with whips of the fire of Hell; and if he commits disobedience with him, Allah will admit him into the Fire."
"1151","""No man is less modest than the one who allows entry into his anus."
"1152","""Whoever deliberately looks at the private parts of his Muslim brother, Allah does not accept his prayer for forty days."
"1153","""Whoever fills his eyes with the forbidden, Allah Almighty will fill his eyes with the embers of Hell."
"1154","""The delegation of Abdul Qais came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him. Among them was a boy with a bright and handsome face, so the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, seated him behind himself and said: 'The sin of Dawud, peace be upon him, was only a glance.'"
"1155","""Do not sit with the children of the wealthy, for their temptation is even more severe than the temptation of virgin girls."
"1156","""Whoever played with chess is accursed."
"1157","""The one who plays chess is like the one who eats the flesh of a pig."
"1158","""The prayer of a man with a sword hanging around his neck is seven hundred times more virtuous than that of a man without a sword hanging around his neck."
"1159","""The angels continuously pray for mercy for the warrior as long as the sword belt remains on his neck."
"1160","""Whoever personally participated in Jihad in the way of Allah, Allah Almighty will forgive him."
"1161","""Whoever fears the fire of Hell for himself should stand guard on the shore for forty days."
"1162","""Whoever says one takbeer in the way of Allah, then (on the Day of Judgment) it will be like a rock in his scale, which will be heavier than the seven heavens."
"1163","""When people accept Islam, they have protected their blood and wealth."
"1164","""Whoever inserts a (third) horse between two horses, and he is not certain that it will win, then there is no harm; but if he is certain, then this is gambling."
"1165","""Indeed, the ruler is Allah's shade and His spear on the earth."
"1166","""When Allah Almighty intends to create a creature for the Caliphate, He passes His right hand over His forehead."
"1167","""People follow the religion of their kings."
"1168","""In the near future, there will be oppressive rulers in the last era; so whoever fears their whip and their sword, let him neither enjoin (good) upon them nor forbid (evil) from them."
"1169","""The supplication of the oppressed is accepted as long as they are not greater in number than the oppressors, and if they are greater in number than them, then their supplication is not accepted."
"1170","""Whoever helps an oppressor, Allah Almighty imposes that (oppressor) upon him."
"1171","""Those who show haste before the king, soldiers of the army, and helpers of the oppressors are dogs of the Fire."
"1172","""Allah's wrath becomes severe upon the one who oppresses a person who has no helper except Allah."
"1173","""O Abu Hurairah! Do not curse the rulers, because Allah Almighty has sent a group into Hell for the reason that they used to curse their rulers."
"1174","""There are twelve Pharaohs: five were in the previous communities and seven will be in my community."
"1175","""Whatever a person uses to protect his honor, it is charity for him."
"1176","""Whoever harms a dhimmi, I will be his opponent on the Day of Resurrection."
"1177","""If you meet the one who collects the tenth (tax), then kill him."
"1178","""Allah Almighty says: Whoever is so occupied with the Qur'an that it distracts him from My remembrance and from asking Me (that is, the person who recites the Qur'an so much that he does not even get the opportunity to ask Allah), then I will grant him better than what I give to those who ask, and the superiority of Allah's Word over all other words is like the superiority of Allah over His creation."
"1179","""No part of the Qur'an suffices as much as Surah Al-Fatihah does, and if Surah Al-Fatihah were placed on one side of the scale and the entire Qur'an on the other side, Surah Al-Fatihah would outweigh the Qur'an seven times."
"1180","""There is a cure for poison in Surah Al-Fatihah."
"1181","""When you lie down on your bed and recite Surah Al-Fatihah and 'Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad', then you are safe from everything except death."
"1182","""Whoever recites Surah Al-Fatiha and Ayat Al-Kursi at home, no human or jinn's evil eye will affect him that day."
"1183","""Surah Al-Fatihah is equal to two-thirds of the Qur'an."
"1184","""Two verses are from the Qur'an; both will intercede, Allah loves them, and both are the last verses of Surah Al-Baqarah."
"1185","""Whoever recites Surah Al-Baqarah will be crowned with a crown in Paradise."
"1186","""Everything has a hump (i.e., the highest point), and the hump of the Qur'an is Surah Al-Baqarah."
"1187","""Whoever recites on Friday the surah in which the family of Imran is mentioned, Allah Almighty will send mercy upon him until sunset, and the angels will pray for mercy for him."
"1188","""The Greatest Name of Allah, with which if supplicated, the prayer is accepted, is in this verse of Surah Aal-e-Imran: «قل اللهم مالك الملك تؤتى الملك من تشاء . . . الخ» ."
"1189","""Whoever mounts a difficult animal and recites this verse (from Surah Al-Imran) into its ear, it will stand still by Allah's command. «افغير دين الله يبغون وله اسلم من فى السموات والأرض طوعا وكرها واليه يرجعون» ."
"1190","""Allah Almighty will not deprive the servant who stands for prayer during the night and begins with Surah Al-Baqarah and Surah Aal-e-Imran. Surah Al-Baqarah and Surah Aal-e-Imran are a person's best treasure."
"1191","""Recite Surah Hud on Fridays."
"1192","""Sūrah Hūd and other sūrahs like it (which contain descriptions of the Day of Judgment), such as al-Wāqi‘ah, al-Qāri‘ah, al-Ḥāqqah, Idhā ash-Shamsu Kuwwirat, and Sāla Sā’il and others, have made me old."
"1193","""The name of Surah Kahf in the Torah is 'Ha'ilah' because this Surah becomes a barrier and obstruction between its reciter and the fire of Hell."
"1194","""Whoever recites the first three verses of Surah Al-Kahf will be protected from the trial of Dajjal."
"1195","""Shall I not tell you of a surah whose greatness fills the space between the heavens and the earth, and for the one who recites it, there is an equal reward, and whoever recites it will have his sins forgiven until the next Friday and for three more days? The companions, may Allah be pleased with them, said: 'Certainly, do tell us.' So he, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Surah Al-Kahf."
"1196","“Allah Almighty recited Surah Ta-Ha and Surah Ya-Sin a thousand years before the creation of the heavens and the earth. When the angels heard the Qur’an, they said: Glad tidings to the nation upon whom this Qur’an will be revealed.”"
"1197","""Whoever recites Surah Yaseen for the pleasure of Allah, Allah Almighty will forgive his previous sins."
"1198","""Whoever begins the day by reciting Surah Yaseen, his needs are fulfilled."
"1199","""Whoever recites Surah Ad-Dukhan on the night of Friday will be forgiven."
"1200","""Whoever recites Surah Ad-Dukhan at night, seventy thousand angels begin to seek forgiveness for him."
"1201","""Whoever recites Surah Dukhan in full, the initial verses of Ha Meem Ghafir up to «واليه المصير» , and Ayat al-Kursi in the evening, will be protected through them until morning; and whoever recites them in the morning will be protected until evening."
"1202","""Whoever says this three times in the morning: «اعوذ بالله السميع العليم من الشيطان الرجيم» and recites the last three verses of Surah Al-Hashr, Allah Almighty will appoint seventy thousand angels for him who will pray for mercy for him until evening, and if he dies that day, he will die the death of a martyr. And whoever says these words in the evening will also attain this rank."
"1203","""Whoever recited the last verses of Surah Al-Hashr during the night or day, and then died that same night or day, Paradise became obligatory for him."
"1204","""The Greatest Name of Allah Almighty is in the last six verses of Surah Al-Hashr."
"1205","""When you lie down on your bed, recite Surah Hashr. (Then) if you die, you will die the death of a martyr."
"1206","""Teach Surah Al-Waqi'ah to your women; indeed, it is the Surah of richness and prosperity."
"1207","""Whoever recites Surah Waqiah and learns it will not be written among the heedless, and his household will not be in need."
"1208","""Whoever recites Surah Al-Waqi'ah every night will never experience poverty."
"1209","""Surah «اذا زلزلت» is equal to half of the Qur'an."
"1210","""Whoever recites Surah «الم نشرح» and Surah «الم تركيف» in the Fajr prayer will not be destroyed."
"1211","""Reciting Surah «انا انزلناه» after ablution."
"1212","""Whoever recites Surah «انا انزلناه فى ليلة القدر» once after ablution will be among the truthful. Whoever recites it twice will be recorded among the martyrs, and whoever recites it three times, Allah Almighty will raise him with the prophets."
"1213","""Whoever recites Surah Ikhlas during their terminal illness will not be tested in the grave."
"1214","""Whoever recites Surah Ikhlas twenty times, Allah Almighty will build a palace for him in Paradise."
"1215","""Whoever recites Surah Ikhlas two hundred times, Allah Almighty will forgive two hundred years of his sins."
"1216","""Whoever recites Surah Ikhlas two hundred times during the day, Allah Almighty writes for him fifteen hundred good deeds, unless he is in debt."
"1217","""Whoever passes by graves and recites Surah Ikhlas eleven times, then gifts its reward to the deceased, he will be granted a reward equal to the number of the dead."
"1218","""Whoever recites Surah Al-Ikhlas, Surah Al-Falaq, and Surah An-Naas seven times after the Friday prayer, Allah Almighty will protect him from evil until the next Friday."
"1219","""On the Day of Judgment, every relationship and lineage will be cut off except for my relationship and lineage."
"1220","“Jibreel (peace be upon him) descended upon me and said that Allah Almighty sends you greetings of peace and says: I have made the Fire forbidden for that loins (Abdullah) from which you were emitted, that womb (Aminah) which bore you, and that lap (Abdul Muttalib) which nurtured you.”"
"1221","“Jibreel (peace be upon him) descended upon me and said: O Muhammad! Allah, the Exalted, sends you greetings of peace and says: O My beloved! I adorned Yusuf (peace be upon him) with beauty from the light of My Throne’s footstool, and I adorned your face with beauty from the light of My Throne.”"
"1222","“Jibreel (peace be upon him) came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) with a bunch of grapes and said: Allah Almighty sends you greetings of peace and has sent me with this bunch so that you may eat it.”"
"1223","“My intercession has been accepted for these persons: my father, my uncle Abu Talib, and my foster brother Ibn Sa’diyyah.”"
"1224","""Allah Almighty granted Musa (peace be upon him) the gift of conversation, but He granted me vision (that is, His sight), and He favored me with the Maqam-e-Mahmood and the Hawd-e-Mawrood."
"1225","""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) gave a man the sweat from his arms, and he put it in a bottle until it was filled. Then he would use it as perfume, and the people of Madinah would smell a pleasant fragrance from it."
"1226","""When this verse «اذا جاء نصرالله والفتح» was revealed, Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: O Jibreel! News of my soul's death has been given to me."
"1227","""(O Prophet!) Whoever sends blessings upon you one hundred times in the day and night, I will send mercy upon him two thousand times, and one thousand of his needs will be fulfilled."
"1228","""Whoever sends blessings upon me at my grave, I hear him."
"1229","""I am the first Prophet in terms of creation and the last in terms of being sent."
"1230","""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not pass away until he had learned to read and write."
"1231","""My name in the Qur'an is Muhammad, in the Gospel it is Ahmad, and in the Torah it is Ahid."
"1232","""The Prophet (peace be upon him) forbade disposal two months before his passing."
"1233","""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) secluded himself for worship two months before his passing and also separated himself from women."
"1234","""Recognition is my real wealth, intellect is the foundation of my religion, and lineage is my basis."
"1235","""The Prophet's (peace be upon him) index finger (that is, the forefinger) was longer than the middle finger."
"1236","""I was born during the reign of the just king (that is, Anushirwan)."
"1237","""Do not make me like the cup of a rider (i.e., do not delay in mentioning me, because a rider hangs his cup on the back of his mount. Al-Nihayah)."
"1238","""If you name a child Muhammad, then honor and respect him (do not humiliate him)."
"1239","""The family of Muhammad is the tree of Prophethood, the family of mercy, and the station of Messengership."
"1240","""Whoever harbored enmity against us, the Ahl al-Bayt, Allah Almighty will raise him as a Jew, even if he was regular in prayer and fasting."
"1241","""Our group of people will rise from their graves on the Day of Judgment, despite their sins and faults, with faces shining like the full moon."
"1242","""Allah's wrath is severe upon the one who shed my blood and caused harm to my family."
"1243","""Allah Almighty has created the offspring of every prophet from his own loins, but my offspring He has created from the loins of Ali."
"1244","""If Ibrahim had lived, he would have been a prophet."
"1245","""Allah Almighty says to you that you should marry the daughter of Abu Bakr (Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her)."
"1246","""(Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates that) I gave birth to an incomplete child from the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), so he named him Abdullah and gave me the kunyah Umm Abdullah."
"1247","""O Aisha! You are more excellent than milk."
"1248","""(Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him) How is your love for me? The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, replied: Like the knot of a rope."
"1249","""Acquire half of your religion from Humaira (that is, Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her)."
"1250","""O Ali! Allah Almighty has commanded me to make Abu Bakr a father, Umar an advisor, Uthman a support, and you, O Ali, a helper."
"1251","""On the Day of Resurrection, a caller will announce under the Throne, 'Where are the companions of Muhammad?' Then Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, and Ali (may Allah be pleased with them) will be brought forth."
"1252","""Abu Bakr is my minister and, after me, the guardian of my Ummah; Umar is my beloved, the one who speaks on my behalf; Uthman is from me; and Ali is my brother and the bearer of my banner."
"1253","""On the Day of Resurrection, Allah Almighty will manifest Himself to all of creation in general, and (O Abu Bakr!) He will manifest Himself to you in particular."
"1254","""O Abu Bakr! Rejoice, for the one who made you perform ablution for the prayer was Jibreel (peace be upon him)."
"1255","""When Allah Almighty created the souls, He chose the soul of Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) from among the rest of the souls, and his clay was taken from Paradise."
"1256","""Allah Almighty has made a pavilion of white ruby in the highest place of Illiyin for Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"1257","""When Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) was born, Allah Almighty came near Paradise of Aden and said: 'By My honor and My majesty, I will admit into you only the one who loves this child.'"
"1258","""Allah Almighty has made Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) my successor over religion and divine revelation, so you should obey him."
"1259","“Jibreel (peace be upon him) said to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) regarding Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him): His fame on the earth is less than it is in the heavens.”"
"1260","""Who can be like Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), for when people denied me, he affirmed my truthfulness and believed in me."
"1261","""On the Day of Resurrection, a chair will be set up for Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) and he will sit on it."
"1262","""I was taken up to the sky, and whenever I passed through a heaven, I found my name, Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, and behind it the name of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq written."
"1263","""It is not permissible for any people that while Abu Bakr is present among them, someone else should lead them in prayer."
"1264","""If the faith of Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) were weighed against the faith of all the people of the earth, his faith would outweigh theirs."
"1265","""Whatever Allah Almighty has placed in my chest, He has also placed the same in Abu Bakr's chest."
"1266","""‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would be conversing with Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) and I would be like an Abyssinian between them."
"1267","""Allah Almighty dislikes in the heavens that Abu Bakr Siddiq should make any mistake."
"1268","""If I had not been sent among you, Umar would have been sent."
"1269","""When I was taken on the night journey, I saw in the heavens a (beautiful, winged horse with a head of red ruby)... I asked Jibreel (Gabriel), peace be upon him, 'For whom is this?' He replied: 'For those who love Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both.'"
"1270","""The first person in this Ummah to be given the book of deeds in his right hand will be Umar (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"1271","""O Abu al-Hasan! (that is, Ali, may Allah be pleased with him) Love both of them (that is, Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them). Because of your love for both of them, you will enter Paradise."
"1272","“There are eighty thousand angels in the sky of this world who seek forgiveness for those who love Abu Bakr and Umar (may Allah be pleased with them).”"
"1273","""Whoever abused Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), his abode is Hell."
"1274","""Whoever abuses Abu Bakr and Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) should be killed, and repentance should not be sought from him."
"1275","""On the night of Mi'raj, I saw a green branch in the Throne upon which it was written in white light: There is no deity except Allah, Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr is the Truthful, and Umar is the Discriminator."
"1276","""(On the night of Mi'raj, the Prophet ﷺ asked a houri:) 'For whom are you?' She replied: 'For Uthman ibn Affan, who will attain martyrdom.'"
"1277","""(The Prophet ﷺ did not lead the funeral prayer of a man, so when the Companions inquired about the reason, he explained:) This person used to hate Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him), so Allah also hates him."
"1278","""When Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) moves from one place to another, Paradise shines for him."
"1279","""The Prophet (peace be upon him) stood up, held Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) firmly, then said: 'You are my friend in this world and the Hereafter.'"
"1280","""Every prophet has a close friend (khalil) in his community, and my close friend is Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"1281","""On every leaf of the trees of Paradise, (along with my name) is written 'Uthman Dhu al-Nurayn.'"
"1282","""I, Harun bin Imran, Yahya bin Zakariya, and Ali bin Abi Talib were all created from the same clay."
"1283","""I and Ali were created from the same light."
"1284","""Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I am the servant of Allah, the brother of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and the greatest truthful one (Siddiq Akbar)."
"1285","""(O Ali!) You are the first person who believed in me, and you will be the first person to shake hands with me on the Day of Resurrection, and you are indeed the Siddiq Akbar and Farooq."
"1286","""If they obey him (i.e., Ali, may Allah be pleased with him), then all will enter Paradise."
"1287","""My brother, my minister, my successor among my family, and the best one whom I leave after myself for the repayment of my debts and the fulfillment of my promises is Ali."
"1288","""The first among you to come to me at the Pond and the first among you to accept Islam is Ali ibn Abi Talib."
"1289","""Whoever does not consider Ali to be the best among the people has certainly committed disbelief."
"1290","""Ali is the best among the creation."
"1291","""I am the house of wisdom and Ali is its door."
"1292","“Revelation was being sent down upon the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and his (peace be upon him) head was in the lap of Ali (may Allah be pleased with him). He (Ali) had not performed the Asr prayer until the sun had set. The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked him: ‘Have you prayed?’ He replied in the negative. Upon this, the Prophet (peace be upon him) supplicated to Allah, so the sun was made to rise again for Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) after it had set.”"
"1293","""(O Ali!) Your position with me is like that of Harun with Musa."
"1294","""Even looking at Ali is an act of worship."
"1295","""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered that all the doors opening into the mosque be closed, except the door of Ali (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"1296","""O Ali! It is not permissible for anyone to be in this mosque in a state of impurity except for me and you."
"1297","""The love of Ali consumes sins just as fire consumes wood."
"1298","""Whoever wishes to see the knowledge of Adam, the understanding of Noah, the forbearance of Abraham, the asceticism of John son of Zechariah, and the firmness of Moses son of Imran, peace be upon them, should look at Ali ibn Abi Talib."
"1299","""My name in the Qur'an is «والشمس وضحاها» and Ali's name is «والقمر اذ تلاها» ."
"1300","""The best one whom I appoint as my successor after me is Ali."
"1301","""Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The people have pledged allegiance to Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), although, by Allah, I was more deserving of it than them."
"1302","""The first person to enter through this door will be the Leader of the Believers and the Chief of the Messengers. (Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that) suddenly Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, came through it."
"1303","""Whoever dies and in his heart there is hatred for Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him), then he should die as a Jew or a Christian."
"1304","""Allah Almighty withholds rain from this Ummah due to hatred against Ali (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"1305","""Whoever wishes to hold on to that branch which Allah Almighty has planted with His own hand, let him hold firmly to the love of Ali."
"1306","""(O Messenger of Allah!) Who will hold your flag on the Day of Judgment? He said, Ali."
"1307","""O Allah! Grant Ali such excellence that You have not given to anyone before him nor will give to anyone after him."
"1308","""Three hundred verses were revealed about Ali (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"1309","""O Ali! Allah Almighty has forgiven you, your children, your parents, your family, your Shia (group), and those who love your Shia."
"1310","""Whoever loves me should love Ali, and whoever harbors enmity towards Ali has harbored enmity towards me."
"1311","""He will certainly not die except that he will be martyred; it refers to Ali (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"1312","""Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I gave the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) the ritual bath, and I drank the water that flowed from the sockets of his eyes, so I was made the inheritor of the knowledge of the first and the last."
"1313","""On the Day of Resurrection, Allah Almighty will say to me and Ali: 'Admit into Paradise those who loved both of you, and admit into Hell those who hated both of you.'"
"1314","""O Ali! You and your Shia (your group) will be in Paradise."
"1315","""My example is like that of a tree: I am its root (origin), and Ali is its branch (trunk, etc.)."
"1316","""Allah Almighty commanded the Prophet (peace be upon him) to eat the fresh dates of Paradise from the platter which Jibreel (peace be upon him) brought to him, and then to have relations with Khadijah (may Allah be pleased with her). (So he did so), and thus Khadijah (may Allah be pleased with her) conceived Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her)."
"1317","""When I was taken on a journey to the heavens, Gabriel (peace be upon him) made me enter Paradise and gave me an apple. I ate it, and it became a seed in my back. When I descended, I had intercourse with Khadijah, and Fatimah is from that seed."
"1318","""I, Fatimah, and Ali will be in Paradise in a white tent whose roof will be the Throne of the Most Merciful."
"1319","""I have been commanded by Allah Almighty to marry Fatimah to Ali, so I have done so."
"1320","""O Ali! Allah Almighty has married you to Fatimah and has set her dowry as the earth, therefore whoever walks on it harboring hatred towards you, will walk upon it unlawfully."
"1321","""When the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) married Fatimah to Ali, he delivered the sermon as follows «الحمد لله المحمود بنعمته المعبود بقدرته . . . »"
"1322","""Gabriel (peace be upon him) delivered a sermon in the heavens and married Fatimah to Ali."
"1323","“When Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her) was sent to Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), Gabriel (peace be upon him) was on the right side before the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), Michael (peace be upon him) was on the left side, and seventy thousand angels were behind them, glorifying and sanctifying Allah Almighty until dawn broke.”"
"1324","""My daughter Fatimah is a human houri; she has never menstruated, and her name is Fatimah (the one who saves) because Allah Almighty has freed her and those who love her from Hell (i.e., has set them free)."
"1325","""Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her) safeguarded her honor, therefore Allah made the Fire of Hell forbidden for her and her offspring."
"1326","""(My daughter Fatimah will hold onto the leg of the Throne and say: O Just and Fair Lord! Decide between me and the killer of my son.)"
"1327","""On the Day of Resurrection, a caller will announce from behind the veils: O people of this gathering! Keep your gazes lowered until Fatimah bint Muhammad (peace be upon him) passes by."
"1328","“Gabriel (peace be upon him) came to me and said that Allah Almighty loves Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her).”"
"1329","""Whoever loves me should love Ali, and whoever loves Ali should love Fatimah."
"1330","""(On the Day of Resurrection) Paradise will say: O Lord! Did You not promise me that You would adorn me with Your two pillars? Then Allah, the Exalted, will say: Did I not adorn you with Hasan and Husayn?"
"1331","""O Gabriel! I have given (my son) Ibrahim as a ransom for Husayn."
"1332","""(O Husayn!) May Allah curse your killer. Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) asked, 'Who will kill him?' The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'A person from my own Ummah who will hate my progeny; he will not receive my intercession.'"
"1333","""Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib is my father, my uncle, my executor, and my heir."
"1334","""My uncle Abbas kept his private parts chaste both in the time of ignorance and in Islam, therefore Allah Almighty has made his body forbidden for the Fire."
"1335","""I saw Abdur Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) entering Paradise crawling on his buttocks."
"1336","""The Prophet (peace be upon him) took the pen from Ali's hand and handed it over to Muawiyah."
"1337","""A group from Banu Hashim requested the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) to relieve Muawiyah from writing down the revelation, so a revelation was sent down regarding his appointment."
"1338","""The first to dispute before the Lord from this Ummah will be Ali and Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with them both)."
"1339","""(Jibreel, peace be upon him, said to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that Allah Almighty says) O My beloved! I have sent this pen as a gift to Muawiyah from above My Throne."
"1340","""The Prophet (peace be upon him) consulted Jibreel (peace be upon him) regarding Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him), so he said, 'Have him write (the revelation), indeed he is trustworthy.'"
"1341","""There are three trustees with Allah: myself, Jibreel (peace be upon him), and Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"1342","""Call Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) to me... Surely, he is strong and trustworthy."
"1343","""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) handed a spear to Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: 'Hold on to it until you meet me in Paradise with it.'"
"1344","""The Prophet (peace be upon him) gave Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) three registers and said, 'You will meet me in Paradise with these.'"
"1345","""Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) will be raised on the Day of Resurrection and there will be a cloak of the light of faith upon him."
"1346","""Every nation has a Pharaoh, and the Pharaoh of this nation is Muawiyah."
"1347","""When you see Muawiyah delivering a sermon from my pulpit, then kill him."
"1348","""Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with him) is the most forbearing and generous among my Ummah."
"1349","""Indeed, for my Ummah, the heat of Hell will be like the heat of a bathhouse."
"1350","""Paradise will remain forbidden to all nations until I and my Ummah enter it."
"1351","""My Ummah is a blessed Ummah; there is no punishment for it in the Hereafter (rather) they are only given punishment in this world in the form of earthquakes and tribulations (etc.)."
"1352","“Love the Arabs for three reasons: I am an Arab, the Qur’an is in Arabic, and the language of the people of Paradise is Arabic.”"
"1353","""The best people are the Arabs, the best among the Arabs are the Quraysh, and the best among the Quraysh are the Banu Hashim."
"1354","""There are armies of Allah in the heavens and on the earth; the heavenly armies of Allah are the angels, while the armies on earth are the people of Khurasan."
"1355","""The worst speech in the sight of Allah is Persian."
"1356","""When Allah Almighty is pleased, He reveals in Arabic, and when He is displeased, He reveals in Persian."
"1357","""Whoever among you can speak good Arabic should never speak Persian, because Persian leads to hypocrisy."
"1358","""Eliminate the customs of the non-Arabs and revive the customs of the Arabs."
"1359","""Whoever lets an Abyssinian enter his house, Allah Almighty will bring blessings into his house."
"1360","""When an Abyssinian is satiated, he commits adultery, and when he is hungry, he steals."
"1361","""Beware of the Jews and Hindus, even if with seventy stomachs."
"1362","""There are some angels of Allah who transfer the deceased."
"1363","""There is an angel of Allah whose distance between the corners of both eyes is a journey of five hundred years."
"1364","""There is an angel of Allah whose upper half is of ice and lower half is of fire."
"1365","""The muezzin of those in the heavens is Jibreel (peace be upon him), and their imam is Mikaeel (peace be upon him)."
"1366","""Tie the lower garment in the manner I have seen the angels tying it before their Lord, up to the middle of the shins."
"1367","""Apply dye to your beards, for surely the angels are pleased with the dye of a believer."
"1368","""When one of you approaches his wife (for intercourse), he should cover himself, for if he does not cover himself, the angels will leave out of modesty and Satan will be present. Then, if a child is destined for them, Satan will have a share in him."
"1369","""When Allah Almighty loves a servant, He instills his love in the hearts of the angels as well."
"1370","""When one of you sneezes and says 'Alhamdulillah', the angels say 'Lord of the worlds'. And if he also says 'Lord of the worlds', then the angels say 'May Allah have mercy on you'."
"1371","""On the day of Friday, the devils head towards the markets in the morning, casting nets of deceit and trickery upon the people and preventing them from attending the Friday prayer. And the angels come and sit at the doors of the mosques in the morning (and record the names of those who attend the Friday prayer)."
"1372","""When someone dies, the angels say, 'What has he sent ahead?' And people say, 'What has he left behind?'"
"1373","""Whoever prays abundantly, the angels say: The voice has been recognized, the prayer has been accepted, and the need has been fulfilled."
"1374","""Select an imam with care; the one who leads you in prayer should be the best among you. Indeed, Allah also selects messengers from among the angels and humans."
"1375","""The best form of guarding (i.e., keeping watch) is adherence to prayer and gatherings of remembrance, and whoever, after performing prayer, remains seated at the place of prayer, as long as he does not lose his ablution or stand up, the angels continue to pray for mercy upon him."
"1376","""A side-lying grave was made for Adam (peace be upon him), and he was washed with water an odd number of times. So the angels said: This is the Sunnah for the children of Adam after him."
"1377","“The angels bathed Adam (peace be upon him) with water and leaves of the lote tree, shrouded him, made a side grave for him, and said: O children of Adam! This is your tradition regarding your deceased.”"
"1378","""When someone eats in the presence of a fasting person, the angels pray for mercy for him."
"1379","""O Bilal! When food is eaten in the presence of a fasting person, his bones declare tasbih and the angels seek forgiveness for him."
"1380","""Allah Almighty boasts to the angels about a devout young person and says, 'Look at My servant; he has abandoned his desires for My sake.'"
"1381","""The angels shake hands with the riders among the pilgrims and embrace those who walk on foot."
"1382","""When the winter season departs, the angels rejoice, showing mercy to the poor Muslims due to the severity of the summer heat."
"1383","""As long as your dining mat remains spread, the angels continue to pray for mercy for you."
"1384","“Angels do not descend upon the people among whom there is a person who severs ties of kinship.”"
"1385","""On the Day of Resurrection, people will be raised in the form of three groups (one of them is) a group whom the angels will be dragging on their faces."
"1386","“We will come to a market (in Paradise) where angels will be standing in rows; no eyes would have ever seen a market like it, nor ears ever heard of it, nor would any hearts have ever conceived of it.”"
"1387","""I saw the angels washing Hanzala bin Abi Amir between the heaven and the earth in a silver vessel with water from the clouds."
"1388","""I saw the angels giving Hamza a bath."
"1389","""Whoever becomes the guardian of the affairs of my Ummah after me will be made to stand on the Bridge of Sirat on the Day of Judgment, and the angels will open his book of deeds. If he is just, Allah Almighty will grant him salvation because of his justice."
"1390","""The angels' gift is to keep the mosques fragrant."
"1391","""With three voices Allah boasts to the angels: the call to prayer (adhan), the takbir in the way of Allah, and the loud recitation of the talbiyah."
"1392","""The houris have been created from the glorification (tasbih) of the angels."
"1393","""I saw that most of the angels I observed were wearing turbans."
"1394","""I asked my Lord to make the Duha prayer obligatory upon my Ummah, but He replied, 'This is the prayer of the angels; whoever wishes may perform it, and whoever wishes may leave it.'"
"1395","""Name (your children) after the names of the Prophets, but do not name (them) after the names of the angels."
"1396","""In the time of the Dajjal, the food of the believers will be the same as the food of the angels, and that is tasbih (glorification) and taqdees (sanctification)."
"1397","""(Allah Almighty says) When My servant reaches the age of seventy years, the angels begin to love him, and when he reaches the age of ninety years, the angels say: This is Allah's prisoner on His earth. Then Allah Almighty forgives all his past and future sins and also accepts his intercession on behalf of his family members."
"1398","""On the day of the Battle of Badr, the sign of the angels was black turbans, while on the day of the Battle of Uhud, it was red turbans."
"1399","""There are three qualities of prayer (one of them is that) the angels surround it from his feet up to the sky."
"1400","""Angels are present with you in only two games: horse racing and archery competitions."
"1401","""Those households to whom a flock of goats returns in the evening, the angels continue to pray for mercy upon them until morning."
"1402","""Whoever sells a defective item and does not disclose its defect, he remains under the wrath of Allah continuously, and the angels continuously curse him."
"1403","""Whoever completes the recitation of the Qur'an at the beginning of the day, the angels pray for mercy upon him until the evening; and whoever completes it at the end of the day, the angels pray for mercy upon him until the morning."
"1404","""Whoever calls a person without his name, the angels curse him."
"1405","""A believer is more honorable in the sight of Allah than some angels."
"1406","""In the house in which there is a bell, angels do not enter."
"1407","""Whoever sets out in the morning to seek knowledge, the angels pray for mercy upon him and blessings are placed in his livelihood."
"1408","""O Abu Hurairah! Teach the Qur'an to the people and learn it yourself as well. Then if you die while you are in this state, the angels will visit your grave just as the Ancient House (Ka'bah) is visited."
"1409","""Whoever breaks the fast of a fasting person in Ramadan with lawful earnings, the angels pray for mercy for him throughout all the nights of Ramadan."
"1410","""Adhere to the use of the miswak; the miswak is the best thing... The angels praise the one who uses the miswak. (By using the miswak) the Lord becomes pleased and Satan becomes displeased."
"1411","""The angels do not pray for mercy for the woman who wails."
"1412","""On the morning of Eid al-Fitr, the angels stand on the sides of the roads and call out: O people! Set out for reward and recompense. Your Lord had commanded you to fast, and you have observed the fasts; now receive its reward. Then, when the people have performed the Eid prayer, a caller announces in the heavens: Return to your homes as those who have been guided; I have forgiven you. In the heavens, this day is named the Day of Reward."
"1413","""None of the children of Hazrat Hawwa (peace be upon her) would survive. When she became pregnant, Iblis circled around her and said: Name him Abdul Harith. They named him Abdul Harith, and he survived."
"1414","""Beware of arrogance, for it was arrogance that incited Iblis to refuse to prostrate to Adam (peace be upon him)."
"1415","""When the enemy of Allah, Iblis, came to know that Allah Almighty had accepted my supplication and forgiven my Ummah, he began to throw dust upon his head."
"1416","""The most back-breaking thing for Iblis is a religious scholar who goes out among the people."
"1417","""Garlic, onion, and leek (a foul-smelling vegetable) are the fragrance of Satan."
"1418","""When any of you leaves the mosque, the army of Iblis turns towards him and gathers around him like bees. Therefore, when someone is about to leave the mosque, he should surely seek refuge from Iblis and his armies."
"1419","“Recite the Kalimah La ilaha illallah and seek forgiveness abundantly, because Iblis says, ‘I destroyed people with sins, and people destroyed me with the Kalimah La ilaha illallah and seeking forgiveness.’”"
"1420","""Whoever manages his wealth well, Satan sends his strongest and most powerful companion towards him."
"1421","""Poetry is the instrument of Iblis."
"1422","""Beware of the world and beware of women. Indeed, Satan is very watchful and lying in wait, and among the pious, there is no snare stronger for his prey than women."
"1423","Iblis said to Allah Almighty: ""O my Lord! Adam has been sent down (to the earth), and I know that soon he will be given books and messengers, so what are his books and messengers?"" Allah Almighty said: ""His messengers are angels and chosen prophets from among them, and his books are the Torah, the Gospel, the Psalms, and the Furqan."" He said: ""And what is my book?"" Allah Almighty said: ""Your book is the leaves of branches, your Quran is poetry, your messengers are soothsayers, your food is that upon which Allah's name has not been mentioned, every intoxicating thing is your drink, your truth is falsehood, your house is the bathhouses, your ambush places are women, your callers to prayer are musical instruments, and your mosque is the marketplace."
"1424","""The first to be clothed with the garments of Hell will be Iblis."
"1425","""Iblis was the first to wail and he was the first to sing."
"1433","""When you perform ablution, do not shake your hands because these (splashes) are the fans of Satan."
"1434","""Women are the snare of Satan."
"1435","""The row that most prevents Satan is the first row."
"1436","“Indecency and immorality are from Satan; these two acts bring one closer to Hell and farther from Paradise.”"
"1437","""Satan is very sensitive and very fond of licking, so protect yourselves from his attacks on your souls. Whoever spends the night and there is the smell of grease on his hand, and then something harms him, then he should only blame himself."
"1438","""Satan is a wolf to humans just as a wolf is to goats; he seizes the goat that separates from the herd. So beware of separating yourselves, and adhere to the congregation, public places, and the mosque."
"1439","""Satan distresses one and two men, but when there are three men, he cannot distress them."
"1440","""Since Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) accepted Islam, whenever Satan met him, he fell on his face."
"1441","""Satan places his bridle upon the heart of the son of Adam; if he remembers Allah, Satan withdraws, but if he forgets, Satan swallows his heart."
"1442","""Satan loves the color red, so avoid red and every garment of fame."
"1443","""Avoid the color red, for it is the adornment most beloved to Satan."
"1444","""Red color is the adornment of Satan."
"1445","""The one who moves up and down before the Imam, his forehead is in the hand of Satan."
"1446","""To eat with one finger is the way of eating of Satan, to eat with two fingers is the way of eating of the rebellious, and to eat with three fingers is the way of eating of the Prophets."
"1447","""Weeping is due to mercy, and wailing and lamentation are from Satan."
"1448","""Severe yawning and severe sneezing are from Satan."
"1449","""Loud laughter is from Satan and smiling is from Allah."
"1450","""No prophet has ever experienced a wet dream; indeed, a wet dream is from Satan."
"1451","""Procrastination is the habit of Satan which he tries to instill in the hearts of the believers."
"1452","""Prayer blackens the face of Satan."
"1453","""Always keep goodness gathered upon your tongue; surely, in this way, you will overcome Satan."
"1454","""Speak less (otherwise) Satan may lead you astray."
"1455","""The evil eye is real; it is brought forth by Satan and the envy of the son of Adam."
"1456","""A servant always remains in ease regarding his religion as long as he does not drink alcohol, but when he drinks alcohol, Allah tears away his veil of modesty, and Satan becomes the guardian of his hearing, sight, and steps. He leads him towards every evil and turns him away from every good deed."
"1457","""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade drinking all the water in one breath like animals and said that this is the way of drinking of Satan."
"1458","""By Allah! Satan kept eating with him continuously until he recited Bismillah."
"1459","""Every house in which there is a white rooster, neither the devil nor a sorcerer comes near it."
"1460","""Clean between your beards and nails, for indeed Satan runs between the flesh and the nails."
"1461","“When (in the Battle of Mu’tah) Ja’far (may Allah be pleased with him) took hold of the flag, Satan came to him and aroused in him the desire for worldly life, making death appear hateful to him. He said, ‘Now you are arousing in me the desire for the world while faith has become firm in the hearts of the believers?’ Saying this, he continued to participate in the battle until he was martyred.”"
"1462","""Some of the snares and traps of Satan are these: denial of Allah's blessings, pride over what Allah has given, arrogance towards Allah's servants, and following desires."
"1463","""The superiority of a scholar over a worshipper is seventy degrees... and the reason for this is that when Satan invents an innovation for the people, the scholar recognizes it and prevents (the people) from it (whereas the worshipper remains unaware of it)."
"1464","""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade leaving rubbish in the room because it is a place where the devil sits."
"1465","""Just as one would like that Satan is not present with him at the time of eating and taking a nap, he should say Salam when entering the house and recite Bismillah when eating."
"1466","“When the son of Adam goes to sleep, the (appointed) angel says to Satan, ‘Show me your record.’ Satan gives him his record, then the angel erases ten evil deeds from Satan’s record for every good deed he finds in (the person’s) record, and writes ten good deeds in their place. Therefore, when any of you is about to sleep, let him say ‘Allahu Akbar’ thirty-three times, ‘Alhamdulillah’ thirty-four times, and ‘Subhanallah’ thirty-three times; these supplications will total one hundred.”"
"1467","“Bad character is a bridle of Allah’s punishment in the nose of the ill-mannered person, and this bridle is in the hand of Satan, (therefore) Satan pulls him towards evil and from evil towards Hell.”"
"1468","""Do not drink from the broken part of a vessel, because Satan drinks from it."
"1469","""The spider is a devil; Allah has disfigured its form, so kill it."
"1470","""Do not call it 'Qaws-e-Qazah' (the shape that appears in the clouds like a bow of different colors), because Qazah is the name of Satan; rather, you should call it 'the bow of Allah.'"
"1471","A companion named his son Hubab. When the Prophet (peace be upon him) came to know, he said: Do not name him Hubab, because Hubab is the name of Satan."
"1472","""Indeed, Shihab is the name of Satan."
"1473","""I have been given superiority over Adam (peace be upon him) with two qualities: (and they are that) my Satan was a disbeliever but Allah Almighty helped me against him until he became a Muslim, and my wives are also my helpers, whereas Adam's (peace be upon him) Satan remained a disbeliever and his wife assisted him in his mistake."
"1474","""Every angel in the sky respects Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), and every devil on earth fears Umar (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"1475","""When an orphan sits at the bowl of a people, Satan also draws near to their bowl."
"1476","""(To the one who, despite having the means, does not keep a wife or a slave woman, the Prophet ﷺ said:) 'You are the brothers of devils.'"
"1477","""Satan sets out towards the markets in the morning carrying his flags; he enters with the first person to enter (the market) and leaves with the last person to leave."
"1478","""Iblis has some rebellious devils with him; he tells them to lead the pilgrims and the warriors astray from the (straight) path."
"1479","""When you enter your rooms, say Salam (peace); (by doing so) the devils residing in them will leave."
"1480","""Keep your homes illuminated as much as you are able, and the house in which the Qur'an is recited becomes spacious for its inhabitants, its goodness increases, angels are present therein, and devils leave it."
"1481","""Some of Allah's devils are on land; they have no authority over the things in the sea. (Similarly, some of Allah's) devils are in the sea; they have no authority over the things on land."
"1482","""When a person stands for prayer, seven devils stand with him."
"1483","""When you ride these animals, let them rest at different places; do not ride them like devils."
"1484","""Allah Almighty will send a devil with him (the Dajjal) who will speak to the people."
"1485","""O Abu Dharr! Seek Allah's protection from the devils among the jinn and mankind."" I said, ""(O Messenger of Allah!) Are there also devils among humans?"" He (peace be upon him) said, ""Yes."
"1486","""Iblis came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and asked him about many things, and at that time he was in the mosque with a group of his companions."
"1487","""The death of a religious scholar is, in the eyes of Iblis, better than the death of seventy worshippers."
"1488","""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the sacrifices made for the jinn. (This is the sacrifice that a person performs after building a house with the intention that by doing so, the jinn will not harm the people of his household.)"
"1489","“Jibreel (peace be upon him) came to me and said: A rebellious jinn intends evil against you, so when you lie down on your bed, recite Ayat al-Kursi.”"
"1490","""Muslim and polytheist jinn came to me and argued. They requested me to provide them with a place to live, so I allotted the Muslim jinn to reside in Jalas (mountains and settlements) and the polytheist jinn to reside in Ghawr (the area between mountains and seas)."
"1491","""Keep yourself and your family indoors at the beginning of the evening, for at that time the jinn are out and about."
"1492","""Allah Almighty created the jinn in three types: in the form of snakes, scorpions, and insects of the earth; those like the wind in the air; and those from whom reckoning will be taken and punishment will be given."
"1493","""Ghilan (a special type of jinn) are the sorcerers among the jinn."
"1494","""Everything knows that I am the Messenger of Allah except the disbelieving jinn and disbelieving humans."
"1495","""The disease of plague is the sting of your jinn brothers."
"1496","“Impurity has seventy parts; only one part is among the jinn and humans, and the remaining sixty-nine (69) parts are among the Berber (a nation of North-West Africa).”"
"1497","“When a woman leaves her house while her husband dislikes her going out, then until she returns, every angel in the sky and everything she passes by curses her, except for jinn and humans.”"
"1498","""If all humans, jinn, devils, and angels from the beginning of creation until the Day of Judgment were to stand in a single row, even then they could not encompass Allah Almighty."
"1499","""Do you know what Khurafah (falsehood) is? Khurafah was a man from Banu Udhrah whom the jinn had captured. He remained among them for a long time, then they returned him to the humans. He used to narrate to people the strange things of the jinn which he had seen among them, so people began to say, 'These are Khurafah's tales' (i.e., he is telling false stories)."
"1500","“Jinn do not harm a person in whose house there is a fine horse.”"
"1501","""Whoever enters Paradise, two houris with beautiful eyes will sit by his head and two by his feet, and they will sing to him in the best of voices, which will be heard by both jinn and humans."
"1502","""The Hour will not be established until among you, from your women, a great number of offspring of the jinn will be born (and they will turn you away from your religion)."
"1503","""(Allah Almighty cursed the jinn and transformed them into the form of cattle) These black dogs are actually jinn."
"1504","""The believing jinn will also receive reward, and they will also be punished."
"1505","""(When your uncle intended to send someone for the Prophet's (ﷺ) protection, he said:) O my uncle! Allah Almighty has protected me from the evil of jinn and humans."
"1506","""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade marrying certain women."
"1507","""Human devils are dominant over jinn devils."
"1508","""For protection from the evil eye, there are eight verses in the Book of Allah. Whoever recites them in his house, neither humans nor jinn can cast the evil eye on the people of that house on that day. Seven verses are from Surah Al-Fatiha, and one verse is Ayat al-Kursi."
